.TH SONGBIRD-CONFIG 1 "January 2025" "songbird-orchestrator 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
songbird-config \- Configuration management commands for Songbird Orchestrator
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B songbird config
[\fI\,OPTIONS\/\fR] \fI\,COMMAND\/\fR [\fI\,ARGS\/\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
The config subcommand provides configuration management for Songbird Orchestrator, including initialization, validation, and modification of configuration files.

.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B init
Initialize a new configuration file with defaults
.TP
.B validate
Validate the current configuration file
.TP
.B show
Display the current configuration
.TP
.B set
Set a configuration value
.TP
.B get
Get a configuration value
.TP
.B reset
Reset configuration to defaults
.TP
.B backup
Create a backup of the current configuration
.TP
.B restore
Restore configuration from a backup

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help information
.TP
.BR \-\-config " " \fI\,FILE\/\fR
Specify configuration file path
.TP
.BR \-\-format " " \fI\,FORMAT\/\fR
Output format for show command (toml, json, yaml)
.TP
.BR \-\-environment " " \fI\,ENV\/\fR
Specify environment (development, production, testing)

.SH CONFIGURATION SECTIONS
.TP
.B [network]
Network configuration including bind addresses and ports
.TP
.B [gaming]
Gaming-specific configuration for protocol detection
.TP
.B [security]
Security settings including authentication and encryption
.TP
.B [logging]
Logging configuration and output settings
.TP
.B [orchestrator]
Service orchestration settings
.TP
.B [discovery]
Service discovery backend configuration

.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B songbird config init
Initialize a new configuration file with defaults
.TP
.B songbird config init --environment production
Initialize production-ready configuration
.TP
.B songbird config validate
Validate the current configuration file
.TP
.B songbird config show
Display the entire current configuration
.TP
.B songbird config show --format json
Display configuration in JSON format
.TP
.B songbird config get network.bind_address
Get the current bind address setting
.TP
.B songbird config set network.bind_address 0.0.0.0
Set the bind address to accept connections from any interface
.TP
.B songbird config set gaming.enabled true
Enable gaming protocol detection
.TP
.B songbird config backup
Create a backup of the current configuration
.TP
.B songbird config reset
Reset all configuration values to defaults

.SH CONFIGURATION FILE FORMAT
Configuration files use TOML format:

.nf
[network]
bind_address = "127.0.0.1"
port = 8080
enable_tls = false

[gaming]
enabled = true
detection_timeout = 10
supported_protocols = ["ipx", "directplay", "netbios"]

[security]
authentication_required = false
enable_encryption = true

[logging]
level = "info"
file_path = "/var/log/songbird/songbird.log"
.fi

.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/songbird/config.toml
Main configuration file
.TP
.I ~/.config/songbird/networks.toml
Network-specific configuration
.TP
.I ~/.config/songbird/security.toml
Security configuration
.TP
.I ~/.config/songbird/backups/
Configuration backup directory

.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SONGBIRD_CONFIG_PATH
Override default configuration file path
.TP
.B SONGBIRD_ENVIRONMENT
Set environment mode (development, production, testing)
.TP
.B SONGBIRD_LOG_LEVEL
Override logging level from configuration

.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success
.TP
.B 1
Configuration error
.TP
.B 2
File not found
.TP
.B 3
Permission denied
.TP
.B 4
Validation failed

.SH NOTES
Configuration changes may require a restart of running Songbird services to take effect.

Some configuration options require elevated privileges, particularly those related to network interfaces and packet capture.

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR songbird (1),
.BR songbird-gaming (1),
.BR toml (5)

